# Per-message egress stream selection (SMTP-Send, added 2026-09-08).
#
# Consulted ONLY by cleanup_stream, the cleanup service behind the
# 127.0.0.1:10026 tracking re-injection listener -- so only mail that entered
# through an authenticated submission port and passed the tracking filter can
# ever match. Port 25 uses the default cleanup and never sees this file: an
# outside sender spoofing the header cannot reroute inbound mail (a FILTER on
# an inbound message would try to SMTP-relay a local delivery -- the
# transport_cutover loop-bounce, again).
#
# Why per-message at all: the org-profile sender_dependent transport map keys
# on sender DOMAIN, which cannot split a 'both'-profile org's campaigns from
# its transactional app mail -- found live 2026-09-08 when a campaign left on
# the transactional IP. Campaign sends (and any API caller passing
# stream=marketing) carry this header; everything else falls through to
# default_transport on the primary IP.
#
# Why this must NOT match on the first pass (submission's own cleanup): a
# header_checks FILTER overrides content_filter, which would silently skip
# tracking/List-Unsubscribe injection for exactly the mail that needs it most.
/^X-Mailyte-Stream:\s*marketing\s*$/i FILTER marketing:
